  Derived:
    compute capability 7.5  ->  16 SMs x 64 FP32 lanes = 1024 'CUDA cores'
    Each SM: 4 warp schedulers; a warp = 32 threads executing one instruction (SIMT).
    Register file per SM = 65536 x 32-bit registers, shared by all resident threads:
      a kernel using R regs/thread can keep at most floor(65536/(R*32)) warps per SM.
    FP32 peak = SMs*lanes*2(FMA)*clock = 4.30 TFLOPS at 2100 MHz
    DRAM peak = mem_clock*2*bus/8     = 128.0 GB/s  (128-bit bus)
    PCIe Gen3 x16 = 15.76 GB/s per direction (128b/130b encoding)

